IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nii-il04-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-j-tables`

-- National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], Schedule J (לוח י׳) — THE RULES: which version
-- of the schedule governs a contribution month, how a figure is read out of it, and what its
-- column headings say a figure is applied to. The figures themselves are data, generated from the
-- source into nii-schedule-j-tables.l4. Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt.

§ `Schedule J — rates of insurance contributions`
-- src:4709 | לוח י׳ [תיקון: תשנ״ז, תשס״ב־6, תשס״ג־3, תשס״ג־10, תשס״ה־3, תשס״ה־6, תשס״ה־7, תשס״ו־5]
-- src:4710 | [note: (סעיפים 28, 32 ו־337 עד 342)]
-- src:4711 | שיעור דמי ביטוח בעד אפריל שנת 2011 ואילך [תיקון: תשס״ט־4]

§§ `Which version governs a contribution month`

-- The schedule is printed twice. The first table is labelled by the editors a temporary provision
-- for 2025-2026, the second "the permanent text". Item 4 (work injury) and the totals row of each
-- carry a further editors' note: "(temporary provision in the years 2024 to 2027: …)".
-- src:4714 | [note: (הוראת שעה לשנים 2025–2026):]
-- src:4732 | [note: (הנוסח הקבוע):]
-- REPAIRED 2026-10-07 against the enacted amending Laws (NOTES.md, "Repair 2026-10-07"). The labels
-- and notes are the editors'; each now has an enacted source:
-- * Amendment 252 and temporary provision, 5785-2025 (Sefer HaChukim 3347, pp. 176-177; PDF at
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/amending-laws/25_lsr_5482787.pdf): s 6 commences on 1 January
--   2025; s 7(a) reads the Law, "for national insurance contributions collected in respect of the
--   years 2025 and 2026", until 31 December 2026, with the LOWER sub-columns of columns C and D of
--   Schedule J replaced by new figures (s 7(a)(3)); the upper sub-columns are not replaced. s 7(b)
--   lets the Minister of Finance extend that period by order to 2027 and then 2028, one year at a
--   time.
-- * The Law for the 2025 budget year, 5785-2025 (Sefer HaChukim 3384, pp. 395-396; PDF at
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/amending-laws/25_lsr_6133485.pdf): s 19(6) replaces "60% of the
--   average wage" with "the reduced collection threshold as defined in s 334(a)" everywhere in
--   Schedule J; s 20(1) changes item 2's figure for those who are neither, in the temporary lower
--   sub-column, from 0.17 to 0.16; s 21: both commence on 1 January 2026.
-- * The Economic Efficiency Law (budget years 2023 and 2024), 5783-2023, s 24 (Sefer HaChukim
--   3045, p. 169; fetched 2026-10-06 21:39:39Z through the Israeli proxy, sha256 6d90d3c4...74af,
--   NOTES.md section 7): from 1 January 2024 to 31 December 2027, item 4 for an employee reads 2.06
--   above and 0.47 below the split (for 1.96 and 0.37), and the totals 14.60 and 3.85 to 3.95.
--
-- So, by the year of the contribution month, and by whether an order under Amendment 252 s 7(b)
-- extended the temporary provision to that year (an input; the year-only rule assumes no order,
-- NOTES.md assumption A8):
--   2026        the temporary lower sub-columns (with 0.16), the upper ones with item 4 at 2.06;
--   2027        no order: the permanent table with item 4 at 2.06 and 0.47;
--               an order: the temporary lower sub-columns, the upper ones with item 4 at 2.06;
--   2028        no order: the permanent table as printed; an order: the temporary lower
--               sub-columns, the upper ones as printed (the 2024-2027 figures have lapsed);
--   2029 on     the permanent table as printed; s 7(b) cannot reach these years;
--   before 2026 declined (A1): the 2025 text differs (item 2, 0.17; every heading "60% of the
--               average wage"), and the rest of the 2025 Law is not encoded here. The 2025 lower
--               sub-columns as enacted are kept below as data.
-- In every version read for 2026 on, column D's upper part begins at the reduced collection
-- threshold (fork F3, repaired): Amendment 252 never replaced that sub-column, and s 19(6) amended
-- its heading. The heading the consolidation prints in the temporary table (line 4718, "above 60%
-- of the average wage") is a stale copy of the pre-2026 text; it is quoted, not followed.

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, temporary version (source lines 4714-4730), with the 2024-2027 figures at lines 4723 and 4730 (Economic Efficiency Law 5783-2023 s 24); Amendment 252 s 7(a)(3); 2025 budget-year Law ss 19(6), 20(1), 21
GIVETH A `A version of Schedule J`
`Schedule J, the temporary version for 2025-2026, as read in 2024-2027` MEANS
    `A version of Schedule J` WITH
        `name`   IS "Schedule J, the temporary version for 2025-2026, as read in 2024-2027"
        `rows`   IS `Schedule J (temporary version), items as read in 2024-2027`
        `totals` IS `Schedule J (temporary version), totals as read in 2024-2027`
        `column D upper part begins above 60% of the average wage` IS FALSE

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, temporary version (source lines 4714-4730), as printed; Amendment 252 s 7(a)(3); 2025 budget-year Law ss 19(6), 20(1), 21
GIVETH A `A version of Schedule J`
`Schedule J, the temporary version for 2025-2026, as printed` MEANS
    `A version of Schedule J` WITH
        `name`   IS "Schedule J, the temporary version for 2025-2026, as printed"
        `rows`   IS `Schedule J (temporary version), items as printed`
        `totals` IS `Schedule J (temporary version), totals as printed`
        `column D upper part begins above 60% of the average wage` IS FALSE

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, permanent version (source lines 4732-4748), with the 2024-2027 figures at lines 4741 and 4748 (Economic Efficiency Law 5783-2023 s 24)
GIVETH A `A version of Schedule J`
`Schedule J, the permanent version, as read in 2024-2027` MEANS
    `A version of Schedule J` WITH
        `name`   IS "Schedule J, the permanent version, as read in 2024-2027"
        `rows`   IS `Schedule J (permanent version), items as read in 2024-2027`
        `totals` IS `Schedule J (permanent version), totals as read in 2024-2027`
        `column D upper part begins above 60% of the average wage` IS FALSE

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, permanent version (source lines 4732-4748), as printed
GIVETH A `A version of Schedule J`
`Schedule J, the permanent version, as printed` MEANS
    `A version of Schedule J` WITH
        `name`   IS "Schedule J, the permanent version, as printed"
        `rows`   IS `Schedule J (permanent version), items as printed`
        `totals` IS `Schedule J (permanent version), totals as printed`
        `column D upper part begins above 60% of the average wage` IS FALSE

-- THE 2025 TEXT, AS DATA ONLY (Repair 2026-10-07). Amendment 252 s 7(a)(3)(a) as enacted prints
-- item 2's figure for those who are neither, in the lower sub-column, as 0.17; the 2025
-- budget-year Law s 20(1) made it 0.16 from 1 January 2026, which is what the consolidation
-- prints. Amendment 252's printed total for that sub-column is 6.92 throughout, so in 2025 the
-- column's items (0.17 + 1.65 + 0.06 + 1.31 + 0.14 + 3.60 = 6.93) did not meet its total; the
-- s 20(1) correction made them meet it. Every other figure of Amendment 252's sub-columns equals
-- the consolidation's temporary table. In 2025 every heading still said "60% of the average
-- wage" (s 19(6) changed them only from 2026), hence the flag. No year arm selects this version.
@ref National Insurance Law (Amendment 252 and temporary provision) 5785-2025, s 7(a)(3)(a), item 2 (Sefer HaChukim 3347, p. 177); changed by the 2025 budget-year Law s 20(1) from 1 January 2026
GIVETH A `A row of Schedule J`
`Schedule J (temporary version), item 2, as enacted for 2025` MEANS
    `A row of Schedule J` OF 2,  `maternity`, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST 0.16, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST 0.17, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING

@ref National Insurance Law (Amendment 252 and temporary provision) 5785-2025, s 7(a)(3) (Sefer HaChukim 3347, pp. 176-177); the upper sub-columns with the 2024-2027 figures (Economic Efficiency Law 5783-2023 s 24)
GIVETH A `A version of Schedule J`
`Schedule J, the temporary version as enacted for 2025 (data; 2025 is not answered)` MEANS
    `A version of Schedule J` WITH
        `name`   IS "Schedule J, the temporary version as enacted for 2025 (data; 2025 is not answered)"
        `rows`   IS LIST `Schedule J (temporary version), item 1`
                       , `Schedule J (temporary version), item 2, as enacted for 2025`
                       , `Schedule J (temporary version), item 3`
                       , `Schedule J (temporary version), item 4, with the figures noted for 2024-2027`
                       , `Schedule J (temporary version), item 5`
                       , `Schedule J (temporary version), item 6`
                       , `Schedule J (temporary version), item 7`
                       , `Schedule J (temporary version), item 8`
                       , `Schedule J (temporary version), item 9`
                       , `Schedule J (temporary version), item 10`
        `totals` IS `Schedule J (temporary version), totals as read in 2024-2027`
        `column D upper part begins above 60% of the average wage` IS TRUE

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, amendment tags at source line 4713; Amendment 252 s 7(a)(3) (0.17 in 2025); 2025 budget-year Law ss 19(6), 20(1), 21 (from 1 January 2026)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule J as it stood before 1 January 2026 is not in the deposited text` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule J as it stood before 1 January 2026 is not in the deposited text"

@ref National Insurance Law (Amendment 252 and temporary provision) 5785-2025, s 7(b) (Sefer HaChukim 3347, p. 178)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 7(b) of Amendment 252 can extend the temporary provision only to contributions for 2027 and 2028` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 7(b) of Amendment 252 can extend the temporary provision only to contributions for 2027 and 2028"

-- The version for a contribution month, given whether an order under Amendment 252 s 7(b)
-- extended the temporary provision to that year. For 2026 the order is irrelevant (the provision
-- runs to 31 December 2026 by its own terms); for 2029 on an order saying so is outside the
-- power, and is declined; whether a 2028 order presupposes a 2027 one is not checked (fork F20).
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J (source lines 4709-4749); Amendment 252 ss 6-7; Economic Efficiency Law 5783-2023 s 24; 2025 budget-year Law ss 19-21
GIVEN `the year`     IS A NUMBER
      `an order`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A version of Schedule J`
`Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` `the year` `, the temporary provision extended to that year by an order under Amendment 252 s 7(b):` `an order` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the year` AT LEAST 2029 THEN
               IF   `an order`
               THEN `section 7(b) of Amendment 252 can extend the temporary provision only to contributions for 2027 and 2028`
               ELSE `Schedule J, the permanent version, as printed`
           IF `the year` EQUALS   2028 THEN
               IF   `an order`
               THEN `Schedule J, the temporary version for 2025-2026, as printed`
               ELSE `Schedule J, the permanent version, as printed`
           IF `the year` EQUALS   2027 THEN
               IF   `an order`
               THEN `Schedule J, the temporary version for 2025-2026, as read in 2024-2027`
               ELSE `Schedule J, the permanent version, as read in 2024-2027`
           IF `the year` EQUALS   2026 THEN `Schedule J, the temporary version for 2025-2026, as read in 2024-2027`
           OTHERWISE                        `Schedule J as it stood before 1 January 2026 is not in the deposited text`

-- The year-only rule: no extension order (NOTES.md, assumption A8: none was known at retrieval,
-- 2026-10-06, and the temporary provision ends on 31 December 2026 by its own terms).
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J (source lines 4709-4749); Amendment 252 s 7(a)-(b)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A version of Schedule J`
`Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` `the year` MEANS
    `Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` `the year` `, the temporary provision extended to that year by an order under Amendment 252 s 7(b):` FALSE

§§ `Reading a figure out of the schedule`

-- A cell, by column. "–" stays NOTHING.
GIVEN r     IS A `A row of Schedule J`
      `col` IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the cell of` r `in` `col` MEANS
    CONSIDER `col`
    WHEN `column C, above the threshold, employee`            THEN r's `C above the threshold, employee`
    WHEN `column C, above the threshold, self-employed`       THEN r's `C above the threshold, self-employed`
    WHEN `column C, above the threshold, neither`             THEN r's `C above the threshold, neither`
    WHEN `column C, not above the threshold, employee`        THEN r's `C not above the threshold, employee`
    WHEN `column C, not above the threshold, self-employed`   THEN r's `C not above the threshold, self-employed`
    WHEN `column C, not above the threshold, neither`         THEN r's `C not above the threshold, neither`
    WHEN `column D, upper part of the wage`                   THEN r's `D on the upper part of the wage`
    WHEN `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold` THEN r's `D on the part of the wage not above the threshold`
    WHEN `column E`                                           THEN r's `E Treasury allocation`

GIVEN t     IS A `The totals row of Schedule J`
      `col` IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the printed total of` t `in` `col` MEANS
    CONSIDER `col`
    WHEN `column C, above the threshold, employee`            THEN t's `C above the threshold, employee`
    WHEN `column C, above the threshold, self-employed`       THEN t's `C above the threshold, self-employed`
    WHEN `column C, above the threshold, neither`             THEN t's `C above the threshold, neither`
    WHEN `column C, not above the threshold, employee`        THEN t's `C not above the threshold, employee`
    WHEN `column C, not above the threshold, self-employed`   THEN t's `C not above the threshold, self-employed`
    WHEN `column C, not above the threshold, neither`         THEN t's `C not above the threshold, neither`
    WHEN `column D, upper part of the wage`                   THEN t's `D on the upper part of the wage`
    WHEN `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold` THEN t's `D on the part of the wage not above the threshold`
    WHEN `column E`                                           THEN t's `E Treasury allocation`

-- Column C's six cells, named by the column of insured person and the part of the income.
-- src:4717 | פרט | ענף ביטוח | אחוזים מההכנסה או מהשכר לפי סעיפים 337(א) ו־340(א) | הניכוי משכר העובד לענין סעיף 342(ג) באחוזים | הקצבת אוצר המדינה לפי סעיף 32(ג1) |
-- src:4718 | על חלק העולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) | על החלק שאינו עולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) | על חלק השכר העולה על 60% מהשכר הממוצע | על חלק השכר שאינו עולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) |
-- src:4719 | לעובד | לעובד עצמאי | למבוטח שאינו עובד ואינו עובד עצמאי | לעובד | לעובד עצמאי | למבוטח שאינו עובד ואינו עובד עצמאי |
GIVEN `the column` IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      `the part`   IS A `A part of the income`
GIVETH A `A figure column of Schedule J`
`the column C cell for` `the column` `on` `the part` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the part`
    WHEN `the part above the reduced collection threshold` THEN
        CONSIDER `the column`
        WHEN `an employee`            THEN `column C, above the threshold, employee`
        WHEN `a self-employed person` THEN `column C, above the threshold, self-employed`
        OTHERWISE                          `column C, above the threshold, neither`
    WHEN `the part not above the reduced collection threshold` THEN
        CONSIDER `the column`
        WHEN `an employee`            THEN `column C, not above the threshold, employee`
        WHEN `a self-employed person` THEN `column C, not above the threshold, self-employed`
        OTHERWISE                          `column C, not above the threshold, neither`

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J: one item per branch for each column; items 1 and 2 are both maternity, each printing figures only where the other prints "–"
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`more than one item of Schedule J prints a figure for this branch in this column` MEANS
    REFUSE "more than one item of Schedule J prints a figure for this branch in this column"

-- The figure a version prints for a branch in a figure column: the one item of that branch that
-- prints a figure there. Maternity has two items (1 for the employee and the self-employed, 2 for
-- those who are neither), and in every column at most one of them prints a figure; a test checks
-- that for every version, branch and column. NOTHING where no item prints one.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, columns B and C-E (source lines 4716-4729, 4734-4747)
GIVEN v          IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the branch` IS A `A branch of insurance`
      `col`        IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the figure` v `prints for` `the branch` `in` `col` MEANS
    CONSIDER mapMaybe `the cell in this column` (filter `an item of the branch` (v's `rows`))
    WHEN EMPTY               THEN NOTHING
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY EMPTY THEN JUST x
    OTHERWISE                     `more than one item of Schedule J prints a figure for this branch in this column`
    WHERE
        `an item of the branch` r     MEANS r's `branch` EQUALS `the branch`
        `the cell in this column` r   MEANS `the cell of` r `in` `col`

§§ `A dash is not a zero`

-- Where a person pays contributions in a branch (s 335) and the schedule prints "–" in that
-- person's column, the schedule gives no rate; it does not give a rate of 0. One case has its own
-- answer elsewhere in the Law: work injury for an insured person who is neither employee nor
-- self-employed is at rates the Minister sets, not exceeding item 4 (s 340(a)(2), source line 3640,
-- not in this row). Every other dash is declined generically.
@ref National Insurance Law s 340(a)(2) (source line 3640), not in this row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`work-injury contributions of an insured person who is neither employee nor self-employed are at rates the Minister sets under section 340(a)(2), not encoded here` MEANS
    REFUSE "work-injury contributions of an insured person who is neither employee nor self-employed are at rates the Minister sets under section 340(a)(2), not encoded here"

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J: a cell printed "–"
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule J prints no rate for this branch in this column` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule J prints no rate for this branch in this column"

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column C (source lines 4717-4719, 4735-4737)
GIVEN v            IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the branch` IS A `A branch of insurance`
      `the column` IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      `the part`   IS A `A part of the income`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the percentage in column C of` v `for` `the branch` `,` `the column` `,` `the part` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figure` v `prints for` `the branch` `in` (`the column C cell for` `the column` `on` `the part`)
    WHEN JUST p  THEN p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF       `the branch` EQUALS `work injury`
             AND `the column` EQUALS `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed`
        THEN `work-injury contributions of an insured person who is neither employee nor self-employed are at rates the Minister sets under section 340(a)(2), not encoded here`
        ELSE `Schedule J prints no rate for this branch in this column`

§§ `Column C — "on the part above", "on the part not above" the reduced collection threshold`

-- src:4718 | על חלק העולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) | על החלק שאינו עולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) | על חלק השכר העולה על 60% מהשכר הממוצע | על חלק השכר שאינו עולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) |
-- Each figure in column C is a percentage "of the income or the wage under sections 337(a) and
-- 340(a)" and applies "on the part" of it above, or not above, the reduced collection threshold
-- of s 334(a). So the column is MARGINAL (phrasebook 3.6): the part up to the threshold at one
-- figure, the part beyond it at the other. At exactly the threshold all the income is "not above".
-- `the threshold` is an argument: s 334(a) gives it by year (nii-s334-interpretation.l4).
GIVEN `the income`    IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part of` `the income` `not above the threshold` `the threshold` MEANS
    min `the income` `the threshold`

GIVEN `the income`    IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part of` `the income` `above the threshold` `the threshold` MEANS
    max 0 (`the income` MINUS `the threshold`)

-- The contribution in one branch: the figure on each part, as a percentage of that part. Nothing
-- is rounded (NOTES.md, fork F7).
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column C (source lines 4717-4729, 4735-4747); s 337(a)
GIVEN v               IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the column`    IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      `the income`    IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the branch`    IS A `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contribution under` v `for` `the column` `on` `the income` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `in the branch of` `the branch` MEANS
         `the part of` `the income` `not above the threshold` `the threshold`
             TIMES (`the percentage in column C of` v `for` `the branch` `,` `the column` `,` `the part not above the reduced collection threshold`)%
    PLUS `the part of` `the income` `above the threshold` `the threshold`
             TIMES (`the percentage in column C of` v `for` `the branch` `,` `the column` `,` `the part above the reduced collection threshold`)%

-- The contributions in all the branches the person pays (s 335, an input), at the items: their sum.
-- Each branch is listed once (input convention, nii-il04-nouns.l4). Version 0.3.0: this is the
-- items' reading of fork F4 by name; the rule without "at the items" reads the schedule as the
-- switch says (below, "Where the totals row and the items differ").
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column C; s 337(a); s 335 (not in this row) for the branches
GIVEN v               IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the column`    IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      `the income`    IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the branches`  IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contributions under` v `for` `the column` `on` `the income` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `in the branches` `the branches` `, at the items` MEANS
    sum (map `in one branch` `the branches`)
    WHERE
        `in one branch` b MEANS
            `the contribution under` v `for` `the column` `on` `the income` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `in the branch of` b

-- The composite rate on one part of the income across a list of branches, at the items: the sum of
-- the percentages. This is the figure the Institute's rate pages print, and what the tests compare.
-- Version 0.3.0: the items' reading by name; the rule without "at the items" follows the switch.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column C
GIVEN v              IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the column`   IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      `the part`     IS A `A part of the income`
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the combined percentage in column C of` v `for` `the column` `,` `the part` `,` `in the branches` `the branches` `, at the items` MEANS
    sum (map `the percentage for` `the branches`)
    WHERE
        `the percentage for` b MEANS `the percentage in column C of` v `for` b `,` `the column` `,` `the part`

§§ `Column D — the deduction from the employee's wage`

-- src:4717 | פרט | ענף ביטוח | אחוזים מההכנסה או מהשכר לפי סעיפים 337(א) ו־340(א) | הניכוי משכר העובד לענין סעיף 342(ג) באחוזים | הקצבת אוצר המדינה לפי סעיף 32(ג1) |
-- src:4718 | על חלק העולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) | על החלק שאינו עולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) | על חלק השכר העולה על 60% מהשכר הממוצע | על חלק השכר שאינו עולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) |
-- src:4736 | על חלק העולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) | על החלק שאינו עולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) | על חלק השכר העולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) | על חלק השכר שאינו עולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת כהגדרתה בסעיף 334(א) |
-- Column D is the percentage an employer deducts from the employee's wage under s 342(c), which is
-- row IL-05's: who deducts, for which branches, and when. This row encodes what the schedule's
-- headings say the figures apply to. As the consolidation prints them, the two versions differ:
--   temporary version: upper part "on the part of the wage ABOVE 60% OF THE AVERAGE WAGE";
--                      lower part "on the part of the wage not above the reduced collection threshold";
--   permanent version: upper part "on the part of the wage above the reduced collection threshold";
--                      lower part the same.
-- REPAIRED 2026-10-07 (fork F3). On the enacted Laws the temporary version's upper heading is
-- stale: Amendment 252 s 7(a)(3) never replaced the upper sub-column, and the 2025 budget-year Law
-- s 19(6) made its heading "the reduced collection threshold" from 1 January 2026 (s 21). So in
-- every version read for 2026 on the two parts meet at the threshold. Before the repair the rule
-- below declined every 2026 wage above 7,703, on the printed heading (60% of 13,566 is 8,139.6).
-- The refusal stays defined: it is reached only through the 2025 text kept as data, whose headings
-- all said "60% of the average wage", and only if the threshold supplied is not that same figure.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, temporary version, column D headings (source line 4718)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the temporary version of Schedule J prints no column D figure for the part of a wage between the reduced collection threshold and 60% of the average wage` MEANS
    REFUSE "the temporary version of Schedule J prints no column D figure for the part of a wage between the reduced collection threshold and 60% of the average wage"

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column D: a cell printed "–"
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Schedule J prints no column D figure for this branch` MEANS
    REFUSE "Schedule J prints no column D figure for this branch"

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column D (source lines 4718, 4736)
GIVEN v                  IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the threshold`    IS A NUMBER
      `the average wage` IS A NUMBER  @desc the average wage (s 1); not read from 2026: each version selected for 2026 on begins column D's upper part at the threshold (fork F3, repaired), so any figure gives the same answer; only the 2025 text kept as data reads it
GIVETH A NUMBER
`where column D's upper part begins in` v `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `and the average wage at` `the average wage` MEANS
    IF   v's `column D upper part begins above 60% of the average wage`
    THEN 60% TIMES `the average wage`
    ELSE `the threshold`

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column D (source lines 4717-4729, 4735-4747)
GIVEN v            IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the branch` IS A `A branch of insurance`
      `col`        IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the percentage in column D of` v `for` `the branch` `in` `col` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figure` v `prints for` `the branch` `in` `col`
    WHEN JUST p  THEN p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Schedule J prints no column D figure for this branch`

-- The column D amount on a wage, for the branches in which a deduction is made (s 342(c), an
-- input), at the items. Declines a wage that reaches the part the temporary version leaves without
-- a figure. Version 0.3.0: the items' reading by name; the rule without "at the items" follows the
-- switch.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column D (source lines 4717-4729, 4735-4747); s 342(c) (row IL-05) for the branches
GIVEN v                  IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the wage`         IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold`    IS A NUMBER
      `the average wage` IS A NUMBER  @desc the average wage (s 1); not read from 2026: each version selected for 2026 on begins column D's upper part at the threshold (fork F3, repaired), so any figure gives the same answer; only the 2025 text kept as data reads it
      `the branches`     IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the column D deduction under` v `on a wage of` `the wage` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `and the average wage at` `the average wage` `in the branches` `the branches` `, at the items` MEANS
    IF       `the wage` GREATER THAN `the lower of the two edges`
         AND NOT (`the upper part begins` EQUALS `the threshold`)
    THEN `the temporary version of Schedule J prints no column D figure for the part of a wage between the reduced collection threshold and 60% of the average wage`
    ELSE sum (map `the deduction in one branch` `the branches`)
    WHERE
        `the upper part begins` MEANS
            `where column D's upper part begins in` v `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `and the average wage at` `the average wage`
        `the lower of the two edges` MEANS min `the threshold` `the upper part begins`
        `the deduction in one branch` b MEANS
                 min `the wage` `the threshold`
                     TIMES (`the percentage in column D of` v `for` b `in` `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold`)%
            PLUS max 0 (`the wage` MINUS `the upper part begins`)
                     TIMES (`the percentage in column D of` v `for` b `in` `column D, upper part of the wage`)%

§§ `The totals row`

-- Each table closes with a totals row ("סך הכל"). Read as a total, it is the sum of the figures
-- printed above it in that column, a "–" adding nothing. The sum is computed here so the tests can
-- compare it with the printed total; this is the one place a "–" is read as contributing nothing,
-- because that is what a total of printed figures means.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, totals rows (source lines 4730, 4748)
GIVEN v     IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `col` IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum of the items of` v `in` `col` MEANS
    sum (map `the figure or nothing` (v's `rows`))
    WHERE
        `the figure or nothing` r MEANS fromMaybe 0 (`the cell of` r `in` `col`)

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, totals rows (source lines 4730, 4748)
GIVEN v     IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `col` IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the items sum to the printed total of` v `in` `col` MEANS
    `the printed total of` (v's `totals`) `in` `col` EQUALS `the sum of the items of` v `in` `col`

§§ `Where the totals row and the items differ (version 0.3.0)`

-- Fork F4 (NOTES.md): in some cells the printed total is not the sum of the items above it
-- (source lines 4730 and 4748, the totals rows; 2026: column D's upper part 7.00 against 4.67, column C
-- above the threshold for an employee 14.60 against 14.49). Versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 computed from
-- the items and kept the totals as data. RULED by Meng on 2026-10-07, relayed by the lead (backlog
-- row IL-11): the printed totals govern by default; the items' reading is kept, by name, as the
-- alternative of the fork. The rule below is the switch: the other reading is a one-line change.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, totals rows (source lines 4730, 4748); fork F4; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-07
GIVETH A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
`Schedule J — the reading this row takes where its totals row and its items differ` MEANS
    `the printed totals govern`

-- The branches whose items print a figure in a column (maternity once: items 1 and 2 never both
-- print one in a column; a test checks it).
GIVEN v     IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `col` IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
`the branches that print a figure in` v `in` `col` MEANS
    map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `branch`) (filter `prints a figure` (v's `rows`))
    WHERE
        `prints a figure` r MEANS
            CONSIDER `the cell of` r `in` `col`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST x  THEN TRUE

GIVEN v              IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `col`          IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the branches that print a figure in` v `in` `col` `are exactly` `the branches` MEANS
        all (GIVEN b YIELD elem b `the branches`) `printing`
    AND all (GIVEN b YIELD elem b `printing`) `the branches`
    WHERE `printing` MEANS `the branches that print a figure in` v `in` `col`

-- Under the printed totals, a total is the schedule's figure for every branch that prints a figure
-- in its column, together. For fewer branches the schedule prints no total, and where the items do
-- not reach the total it cannot say which item the difference belongs to: declined. Where the items
-- do reach it, the reading changes nothing, for any branches.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, totals rows (source lines 4730, 4748); fork F4
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the printed total of Schedule J in this column is for every branch that prints a figure in it, together; the items do not add up to it, and these are fewer branches` MEANS
    REFUSE "the printed total of Schedule J in this column is for every branch that prints a figure in it, together; the items do not add up to it, and these are fewer branches"

-- What the printed total adds to the items on one part of the income: nothing where the items reach
-- the total, or where the part is nil; for every branch printing a figure, the part times the
-- difference between the printed total and the items' sum; for fewer, declined.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, totals rows (source lines 4730, 4748); fork F4
GIVEN v              IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `col`          IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
      `the part`     IS A NUMBER
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the printed total adds in` v `in` `col` `on a part of` `the part` `for the branches` `the branches` MEANS
    BRANCH IF   `the items sum to the printed total of` v `in` `col`
           THEN 0
           IF   `the part` EQUALS 0
           THEN 0
           IF   `the branches that print a figure in` v `in` `col` `are exactly` `the branches`
           THEN `the part` TIMES (`the printed total of` (v's `totals`) `in` `col` MINUS `the sum of the items of` v `in` `col`)%
           OTHERWISE `the printed total of Schedule J in this column is for every branch that prints a figure in it, together; the items do not add up to it, and these are fewer branches`

-- A combined percentage in one cell, under a reading: the items' sum, or the printed total (for
-- every branch printing a figure there, or where the two agree).
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, totals rows (source lines 4730, 4748); fork F4
GIVEN v              IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `col`          IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
      `the items`    IS A NUMBER
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      r              IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the combined percentage in` v `in` `col` `, whose items sum to` `the items` `for the branches` `the branches` `, reading Schedule J as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the items govern` THEN `the items`
    WHEN `the printed totals govern` THEN
        BRANCH IF   `the items sum to the printed total of` v `in` `col`
               THEN `the items`
               IF   `the branches that print a figure in` v `in` `col` `are exactly` `the branches`
               THEN `the printed total of` (v's `totals`) `in` `col`
               OTHERWISE `the printed total of Schedule J in this column is for every branch that prints a figure in it, together; the items do not add up to it, and these are fewer branches`

§§ `A printed total for fewer branches than it is for (version 0.5.0)`

-- Fork F21 (NOTES.md, "Version 0.5.0"). At the printed totals, where a person pays fewer of the
-- branches that print a figure in a column, and the items there do not reach the printed total,
-- the schedule prints no figure for those branches. In 2026 that is column D's upper part (7.00
-- printed, 4.67 by the items: source lines 4720-4730) and column C above the threshold for an
-- employee (14.60 printed, 14.49 by the items). Versions 0.3.0 to 0.4.1 declined every such case.
-- Three readings, kept by name (nouns): `fewer branches are declined`; `the printed total less the
-- items of the branches not paid`, for any branches; and that reading `for a set the Institute
-- publishes`, every other set declined in the words above. RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (TAKEAWAY):
-- the third, by default, in column D (the employee's deduction). The switch is the rule below;
-- the other readings are a one-line change there, and each has its tests.
--
-- WHY "LESS THE ITEMS NOT PAID". For a person who pays the branches B of those printing a figure
-- in a cell, the printed total less the items of the others is the items of B plus the whole
-- difference between the total and the items: on a part of the wage, the items' deduction plus the
-- part times (total - items), which is how the rules below compute it.
--
-- THE SETS THE INSTITUTE PUBLISHES (the default's criterion). The National Insurance Institute's
-- employees' rates page, as fetched by the second independent tester of row IL-07 (fid-il-13):
--   https://www.btl.gov.il/Insurance/Rates/Pages/%D7%9C%D7%A2%D7%95%D7%91%D7%93%D7%99%D7%9D%20%D7%A9%D7%9B%D7%99%D7%A8%D7%99%D7%9D.aspx
--   2026-10-08T06:29:00Z, sha256 74fc3652d8912f23004b6e2d1d3d7fc39e0fbe928c0b71948ff89e8b71827cf1
--   (re-checked 2026-10-08 against the tester's copy; not deposited, the site reserving its rights).
-- Its form 102 table prints, for contributions from 01.01.2025 (threshold 7,703 from 01.01.2026),
-- the employee's rate with health insurance, up to the threshold / above it; the page's first table
-- prints the employee's health insurance as 3.23% / 5.17% and his National Insurance as 1.04% / 7%.
--   * A controlling shareholder in a closely-held company ("column 2" of form 102): employee
--     4.25% / 11.96%, so National Insurance 1.02% / 6.79%; the page's last table, of National
--     Insurance alone, prints the same controlling shareholder's employee figure as 1.02% / 6.79%.
--     s 335(e) and (f) (source lines 3615-3616) take unemployment and insolvency from a
--     controlling shareholder, "למעט בעל שליטה בחברת מעטים"; insolvency prints no column D
--     figure, so the column D branch not paid is unemployment alone:
--       1.04 - 0.02 = 1.02 and 7.00 - 0.21 = 6.79 (lines 4725, 4730).
--   * Women and men aged 67 to 70 who do not receive an old-age pension ("senior citizen's
--     pension"): employee 3.93% / 10.03%, so National Insurance 0.70% / 4.86% (health taken at
--     the same 3.23% / 5.17%). Past retirement age (s 1, line 130) such a person is not insured
--     under Chapter 6 (s 150, line 1405: "וטרם הגיע לגיל פרישה"), for unemployment (s 158,
--     line 1444, paragraph (1), to the age fixed by Part B of Schedule A1) or under Chapter 9
--     (s 195, line 1929), so s 335(d), (e) and (g) (lines 3614, 3615, 3617) do not reach him; he
--     still pays maternity and senior citizens and survivors (s 335(i), line 3619, while insured
--     under Chapter 11) and long-term care (s 335(h)). The column D branches not paid are accident
--     injury, unemployment and disability:
--       1.04 - 0.03 - 0.02 - 0.29 = 0.70 and 7.00 - 0.07 - 0.21 - 1.86 = 4.86 (lines 4724-4727).
-- Each published rate is the formula exactly. The page also prints a controlling shareholder aged
-- 67 to 70: employee 3.93% / 10.03%, the same set and the same result. The default answers these
-- two sets and declines every other; for a non-resident employee (maternity only, s 335(a)) the
-- formula would give 1.04 - 0.94 = 0.10 and 7.00 - 3.80 = 3.20, a rate the Institute does not
-- publish and the ruling does not accept. The sets are recognised by their branches, in any table
-- (assumed, not ruled: NOTES.md "Version 0.5.0").
-- Column C keeps the decline: the formula does not reach the Institute's National Insurance totals
-- above the threshold for either set (a controlling shareholder: 14.60 - 0.33 - 0.04 = 14.23,
-- where the page's National Insurance table prints 14.17; aged 67 to 70: 14.60 - 2.74 = 11.86,
-- where the page's 16.99 less 5.17 is 11.82), and the ruling is for the employee's deduction.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, totals rows (source lines 4730, 4748); fork F21; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (TAKEAWAY)
GIVETH A `A reading of a printed total of Schedule J where fewer branches are paid than it is for`
`Schedule J — the reading this row takes of a printed total where fewer branches are paid than it is for` MEANS
    `the printed total less the items of the branches not paid, for a set the Institute publishes`

@ref the National Insurance Institute's employees' rates page (fetched 2026-10-08T06:29:00Z, sha256 74fc3652...27cf1), not law; s 335(d)-(h) (source lines 3614-3618); ss 150, 158, 195 (lines 1405, 1444, 1929)
GIVETH A LIST OF (LIST OF `A branch of insurance`)
`the column D branches not paid, for each set whose employee's rate the National Insurance Institute publishes` MEANS
    LIST (LIST `unemployment`)
       , (LIST `accident injury`, `unemployment`, `disability`)

GIVEN v              IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `col`          IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
`the branches that print a figure in` v `in` `col` `and are not among` `the branches` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN b YIELD NOT (elem b `the branches`)) (`the branches that print a figure in` v `in` `col`)

GIVEN `one list`   IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      `other list` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the same branches,` `one list` `and` `other list` MEANS
        all (GIVEN b YIELD elem b `other list`) `one list`
    AND all (GIVEN b YIELD elem b `one list`) `other list`

GIVEN v              IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `col`          IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the National Insurance Institute publishes the employee's rate where the branches of` v `in` `col` `not paid are those not among` `the branches` MEANS
    any (GIVEN s YIELD `the same branches,` s `and` `not paid`)
        `the column D branches not paid, for each set whose employee's rate the National Insurance Institute publishes`
    WHERE `not paid` MEANS `the branches that print a figure in` v `in` `col` `and are not among` `the branches`

-- What the printed total adds to the items on one part of the income, for fewer branches read as
-- f: as `what the printed total adds in` above where the branches are every branch printing a
-- figure, or the items reach the total, or the part is nil; otherwise, by f.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, totals rows (source lines 4730, 4748); fork F21
GIVEN v              IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `col`          IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
      `the part`     IS A NUMBER
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      f              IS A `A reading of a printed total of Schedule J where fewer branches are paid than it is for`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the printed total adds in` v `in` `col` `on a part of` `the part` `for the branches` `the branches` `, fewer branches read as` f MEANS
    BRANCH IF   `the items sum to the printed total of` v `in` `col`
           THEN 0
           IF   `the part` EQUALS 0
           THEN 0
           IF   `the branches that print a figure in` v `in` `col` `are exactly` `the branches`
           THEN `the difference`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER f
               WHEN `fewer branches are declined`
                   THEN `the printed total of Schedule J in this column is for every branch that prints a figure in it, together; the items do not add up to it, and these are fewer branches`
               WHEN `the printed total less the items of the branches not paid`
                   THEN `the difference`
               WHEN `the printed total less the items of the branches not paid, for a set the Institute publishes`
                   THEN IF   `the National Insurance Institute publishes the employee's rate where the branches of` v `in` `col` `not paid are those not among` `the branches`
                        THEN `the difference`
                        ELSE `the printed total of Schedule J in this column is for every branch that prints a figure in it, together; the items do not add up to it, and these are fewer branches`
    WHERE
        `the difference` MEANS `the part` TIMES (`the printed total of` (v's `totals`) `in` `col` MINUS `the sum of the items of` v `in` `col`)%

§§ `Column C and column D under a reading (version 0.3.0)`

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column C; s 337(a); totals rows (source lines 4730, 4748); fork F4
GIVEN v               IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the column`    IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      `the income`    IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the branches`  IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      r               IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contributions under` v `for` `the column` `on` `the income` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `in the branches` `the branches` `, reading Schedule J as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the items govern` THEN `at the items`
    WHEN `the printed totals govern` THEN
             `at the items`
        PLUS `what the printed total adds in` v `in` (`the column C cell for` `the column` `on` `the part not above the reduced collection threshold`)
                 `on a part of` (`the part of` `the income` `not above the threshold` `the threshold`) `for the branches` `the branches`
        PLUS `what the printed total adds in` v `in` (`the column C cell for` `the column` `on` `the part above the reduced collection threshold`)
                 `on a part of` (`the part of` `the income` `above the threshold` `the threshold`) `for the branches` `the branches`
    WHERE
        `at the items` MEANS
            `the contributions under` v `for` `the column` `on` `the income` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `in the branches` `the branches` `, at the items`

-- The rule versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 named, now at the reading the switch names.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column C; s 337(a); the switch above
GIVEN v               IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the column`    IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      `the income`    IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold` IS A NUMBER
      `the branches`  IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contributions under` v `for` `the column` `on` `the income` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `in the branches` `the branches` MEANS
    `the contributions under` v `for` `the column` `on` `the income` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `in the branches` `the branches`
        `, reading Schedule J as` `Schedule J — the reading this row takes where its totals row and its items differ`

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column C; totals rows; fork F4
GIVEN v              IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the column`   IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      `the part`     IS A `A part of the income`
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      r              IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the combined percentage in column C of` v `for` `the column` `,` `the part` `,` `in the branches` `the branches` `, reading Schedule J as` r MEANS
    `the combined percentage in` v `in` (`the column C cell for` `the column` `on` `the part`)
        `, whose items sum to` (`the combined percentage in column C of` v `for` `the column` `,` `the part` `,` `in the branches` `the branches` `, at the items`)
        `for the branches` `the branches` `, reading Schedule J as` r

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column C; the switch above
GIVEN v              IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the column`   IS A `A column of insured persons in Schedule J`
      `the part`     IS A `A part of the income`
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the combined percentage in column C of` v `for` `the column` `,` `the part` `,` `in the branches` `the branches` MEANS
    `the combined percentage in column C of` v `for` `the column` `,` `the part` `,` `in the branches` `the branches`
        `, reading Schedule J as` `Schedule J — the reading this row takes where its totals row and its items differ`

-- Column D: the same, on the wage's two parts (the upper part from where it begins, fork F3).
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column D (source lines 4717-4729, 4735-4747); totals rows (source lines 4730, 4748); fork F4
GIVEN v                  IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the wage`         IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold`    IS A NUMBER
      `the average wage` IS A NUMBER  @desc the average wage (s 1); not read from 2026: each version selected for 2026 on begins column D's upper part at the threshold (fork F3, repaired), so any figure gives the same answer; only the 2025 text kept as data reads it
      `the branches`     IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      r                  IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the column D deduction under` v `on a wage of` `the wage` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `and the average wage at` `the average wage` `in the branches` `the branches` `, reading Schedule J as` r MEANS
    `the column D deduction under` v `on a wage of` `the wage` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `and the average wage at` `the average wage` `in the branches` `the branches` `, reading Schedule J as` r
        `, fewer branches read as` `Schedule J — the reading this row takes of a printed total where fewer branches are paid than it is for`

-- Version 0.5.0: the same, with fork F21's reading for fewer branches given (the form above follows
-- its switch). At the printed totals, the items plus what the printed total adds on each part.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column D (source lines 4717-4729, 4735-4747); totals rows (source lines 4730, 4748); forks F4, F21
GIVEN v                  IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the wage`         IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold`    IS A NUMBER
      `the average wage` IS A NUMBER  @desc the average wage (s 1); not read from 2026: each version selected for 2026 on begins column D's upper part at the threshold (fork F3, repaired), so any figure gives the same answer; only the 2025 text kept as data reads it
      `the branches`     IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      r                  IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
      f                  IS A `A reading of a printed total of Schedule J where fewer branches are paid than it is for`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the column D deduction under` v `on a wage of` `the wage` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `and the average wage at` `the average wage` `in the branches` `the branches` `, reading Schedule J as` r `, fewer branches read as` f MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the items govern` THEN `at the items`
    WHEN `the printed totals govern` THEN
             `at the items`
        PLUS `what the printed total adds in` v `in` `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold`
                 `on a part of` (min `the wage` `the threshold`) `for the branches` `the branches` `, fewer branches read as` f
        PLUS `what the printed total adds in` v `in` `column D, upper part of the wage`
                 `on a part of` (max 0 (`the wage` MINUS `the upper part begins`)) `for the branches` `the branches` `, fewer branches read as` f
    WHERE
        `at the items` MEANS
            `the column D deduction under` v `on a wage of` `the wage` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `and the average wage at` `the average wage` `in the branches` `the branches` `, at the items`
        `the upper part begins` MEANS
            `where column D's upper part begins in` v `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `and the average wage at` `the average wage`

@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column D; the switch above
GIVEN v                  IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `the wage`         IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold`    IS A NUMBER
      `the average wage` IS A NUMBER  @desc the average wage (s 1); not read from 2026: each version selected for 2026 on begins column D's upper part at the threshold (fork F3, repaired), so any figure gives the same answer; only the 2025 text kept as data reads it
      `the branches`     IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the column D deduction under` v `on a wage of` `the wage` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `and the average wage at` `the average wage` `in the branches` `the branches` MEANS
    `the column D deduction under` v `on a wage of` `the wage` `with the threshold at` `the threshold` `and the average wage at` `the average wage` `in the branches` `the branches`
        `, reading Schedule J as` `Schedule J — the reading this row takes where its totals row and its items differ`

-- The combined column D percentage in a cell, under a reading (the items' sum: each branch's figure,
-- a dash declined as for the deduction).
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column D; totals rows; fork F4
GIVEN v              IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `col`          IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      r              IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the combined percentage in column D of` v `in` `col` `for the branches` `the branches` `, reading Schedule J as` r MEANS
    `the combined percentage in column D of` v `in` `col` `for the branches` `the branches` `, reading Schedule J as` r
        `, fewer branches read as` `Schedule J — the reading this row takes of a printed total where fewer branches are paid than it is for`

-- Version 0.5.0: the same, with fork F21's reading for fewer branches given. At the printed totals:
-- the items where they reach the total; the total for every branch printing a figure; for fewer,
-- by f, the items plus the difference (the printed total less the items not paid), or declined.
@ref National Insurance Law, Schedule J, column D; totals rows; forks F4, F21
GIVEN v              IS A `A version of Schedule J`
      `col`          IS A `A figure column of Schedule J`
      `the branches` IS A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
      r              IS A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
      f              IS A `A reading of a printed total of Schedule J where fewer branches are paid than it is for`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the combined percentage in column D of` v `in` `col` `for the branches` `the branches` `, reading Schedule J as` r `, fewer branches read as` f MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the items govern` THEN `the items`
    WHEN `the printed totals govern` THEN
        `the items` PLUS `what the printed total adds in` v `in` `col` `on a part of` 100 `for the branches` `the branches` `, fewer branches read as` f
    WHERE
        `the items` MEANS sum (map (GIVEN b YIELD `the percentage in column D of` v `for` b `in` `col`) `the branches`)
